; 04-and.kurt

; `and` is Kurt's other built-in connective (also declared in `minimal.kurt`).
; Two already-proven facts can always be combined into a conjunction -- the
; rule is called "and-intro", and it is hard-coded, no `load` required:

prop A, B

use A
use B
A and B                 ; "and-intro"

; Splitting a conjunction back into its parts ("and-elim") is *not* built in
; the same automatic way -- you have to state the particular instance you
; need as an axiom yourself:

prop C, D
use C and D
use C and D implies C
C

; Lesson 10 ("load") shows how to pull in the ready-made `propositional` theory, which
; gives you a general `and-elim` (and `or`, `not`, `iff`, ...) once and for
; all, so you no longer have to spell out instances like the one above.
